<main class="page">
  <h1>Isomorphic RPC</h1>
  <p class="lead">An RPC is defined once on the server and called by the same name everywhere — in-process on the server, a fetch in the browser. Reads are cached and coalesced by the underlying <code>memo</code>; mutations post their args and run every call. Live, interactive demos of the whole surface follow.</p>
  <p class="note">Each demo imports its RPC through the <code>$server</code> alias — e.g. <code>import greet from "$server/rpc/greet"</code> resolves to <code>src/server/rpc/greet.ts</code>. The same <code>$server</code> / <code>$ui</code> / <code>$shared</code> aliases work in any <code>.abide</code> or <code>.ts</code> file; see each demo's source tab.</p>
  <ul class="list">
    <li><a href="/rpc/reads">Reads</a> — <code>GET</code>/<code>HEAD</code> and the async-read forms in templates (<code>{'{'}await fn(){'}'}</code>, <code>{'{'}fn.peek(){'}'}</code>, <code>{'{'}#await{'}'}</code>) plus raw bypass and probes.</li>
    <li><a href="/rpc/mutations">Mutations</a> — <code>POST</code>/<code>PUT</code>/<code>PATCH</code>/<code>DELETE</code>, and the full read/mutation symmetry when one opts into caching.</li>
    <li><a href="/rpc/responses">Responses</a> — <code>json</code>, <code>error</code>, <code>error.typed</code> narrowing, <code>redirect</code>.</li>
    <li><a href="/rpc/streaming">Streaming</a> — <code>jsonl</code>/<code>sse</code> consumed with <code>{'{'}#for await{'}'}</code>, chunk probes, streaming mutations, and streaming SSR.</li>
    <li><a href="/rpc/uploads">File uploads</a> — a <code>FormData</code> mutation with file + text validation.</li>
  </ul>
</main>
